  "findings": [
    "Native unarmed PVP HP/attack/defense/speed are approximately 4% above Valter, and the deployed API and actual combat records use those values.",
    "For equal strong decks, the effective linked attack floor is identical (1760%). Linked HP, full opening shield, natural speed and fractional action credit favor Helios. The base attack difference does not produce 4% extra damage per hit once the shared attack floor dominates.",
    "Actual account battles are not equal-deck comparisons: ordinary card types, ICON roles, ordering and pet buffs differ. Helios lost 5 of 15 observed battles against Valter users, including 4 of 7 against Euak.",
    "Fresh controlled PVP: 945 wins / 1536 = 61.5234375%. By higher power groups: 267/512 and 269/512; per-deck groups ranged from 50% to 53.90625%. These are sampled simulations, not live population win rates.",
    "PVP skills are basic-only for both. Both retain 75% personal mitigation, Berkan damage immunity and the same mercenary control/parry/poison protections. PVE skills share total 560% damage, energy 35 and cooldown 5 actions.",
    "Equal additive mercenary equipment dilutes the relative advantage in native defense and linked HP; synthetic gear power 1000000 yields about 2.077% defense advantage, while natural speed and opening ward remain 4%. The inspected three live PVP snapshots had no mercenary equipment.",
    "The audited records retain seed and final fighters, but not complete historical magic/pet input snapshots or attack timeline. Individual critical hits, dodges or last-hit causes cannot be proven from those records. No forced winner or live balance adjustment was made."
